## Z — EXAM PATTERN: Two-Pass Grid Transform with awk

| Construct | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| `lines[NR] = $0` | Store each input line in an array (first pass) |
| `split($0, arr, "")` | Split line into individual characters |
| Track `mincol`, `maxcol`, `minrow`, `maxrow` | Bounding box of the inner `x` rectangle |
| `END { ... }` | Second pass: emit transformed output |
| String concatenation: `out = out "char"` | Build output line char by char |

**Transform rules (in priority order):**
1. If `(row, col)` is inside the inner bounding box → emit `0`
2. Else if char is `*` (outer border) → emit `x`
3. Else → emit the character unchanged (spaces, etc.)

---

## X — LINE BY LINE

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# █ FILLED BY STUDENT: 
awk '
{
  lines[NR] = $0        # save line for second pass
  n = split($0, chars, "")
  for (i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    if (chars[i] == "x") {           # track inner x bounding box
      if (mincol == 0 || i < mincol) mincol = i
      if (i > maxcol) maxcol = i
      if (minrow == 0 || NR < minrow) minrow = NR
      if (NR > maxrow) maxrow = NR
    }
  }
}
END {
  for (r=1; r<=NR; r++) {
    out = ""
    n = split(lines[r], chars, "")
    for (i=1; i<=n; i++) {
      if (r >= minrow && r <= maxrow && i >= mincol && i <= maxcol) {
        out = out "0"     # inside inner bbox: zero it out
      } else if (chars[i] == "*") {
        out = out "x"     # outer border: * becomes x
      } else {
        out = out chars[i]  # spaces and anything else: unchanged
      }
    }
    print out
  }
}
'
```

- First pass accumulates all lines and finds the bounding box of `x` characters
- Second pass (END) replays each line with character-level substitutions
- The bounding box check `r>=minrow && r<=maxrow && i>=mincol && i<=maxcol` correctly fills the ENTIRE inner rectangle region with zeros, not just its border
- `mincol == 0` guard handles the case where no `x` is found (won't happen in valid inputs)

